02:07:41.920 --> 02:07:45.620
He's called Fim... No, he's called Rimbo.

02:07:45.860 --> 02:07:47.400
Yes, he's called Rimbo.

02:07:47.680 --> 02:07:49.920
He's waiting over here. Come and see.

02:07:50.120 --> 02:07:50.280
Oh!

02:07:51.040 --> 02:07:52.320
Pod coming too?

02:07:54.640 --> 02:07:57.070
Hello, um, hello.

02:07:58.130 --> 02:07:59.930
Here's my special friend.

02:08:01.300 --> 02:08:07.940
Hello, I'm Flory, and this is Pom. Say hello, Pom.

02:08:08.420 --> 02:08:09.300
I'm shy.

02:08:10.440 --> 02:08:12.740
Would you like to come to our tea party?

02:08:13.100 --> 02:08:17.140
Oh, yes, please. What's for tea?

02:08:17.560 --> 02:08:22.920
Oh, well, uh, stick biscuits, leaf cakes, mud porridge.

02:08:23.320 --> 02:08:24.000
Mud porridge?

02:08:24.240 --> 02:08:26.680
Oh, yummy, yum, yum. Mud porridge.

02:08:27.080 --> 02:08:28.900
Oh, and apples and crackers.

02:08:29.360 --> 02:08:29.960
Crackers?

02:08:30.000 --> 02:08:32.840
Great! I'm hungry! Let's go!

02:08:33.160 --> 02:08:35.490
Oh, would you like to hear my song first?

02:08:35.790 --> 02:08:39.340
Oh, okay! Then can we eat some crackers?

02:08:40.790 --> 02:08:41.390
Ahem!

02:08:43.820 --> 02:08:49.430
Hello, there's tea for you

02:08:50.260 --> 02:08:52.910
Me lots to drink and lots to eat

02:08:53.610 --> 02:08:55.070
Tea shall treat

02:08:58.650 --> 02:08:59.130
Hello!

02:09:00.000 --> 02:09:04.240
Yes, I'd like to come to you, especially if there's lots for me.

02:09:04.460 --> 02:09:06.600
Lots to drink and lots to eat.

02:09:06.860 --> 02:09:08.610
Oh, how exciting!

02:09:09.280 --> 02:09:09.680
What?

02:09:11.140 --> 02:09:11.900
To eat!

02:09:12.400 --> 02:09:15.590
Would you like to hear it again?

02:09:15.810 --> 02:09:16.530
Oh, yes, please.

02:09:16.790 --> 02:09:17.130
No.

02:09:18.940 --> 02:09:20.380
Let's eat something.

02:09:20.890 --> 02:09:25.140
Oh, yes, a game, a game.

02:09:25.320 --> 02:09:26.460
Can we play a game, Flory?

02:09:26.580 --> 02:09:27.220
Can we, can we?

02:09:27.840 --> 02:09:29.500
Yes, we can, Rockets.

02:09:30.000 --> 02:09:31.080
What shall we play?

02:09:31.840 --> 02:09:34.930
Shhh, toe, toe, toe.

02:09:36.600 --> 02:09:38.920
Toe time, good idea, Pom.

02:09:39.080 --> 02:09:40.720
Let's play tiptoe time.

02:09:41.040 --> 02:09:42.480
Come on, Rimbo.

02:09:42.780 --> 02:09:46.900
OK, but I'm getting very, very hungry.

02:09:48.510 --> 02:09:49.030
This game?

02:09:49.410 --> 02:09:51.390
Oh, Rimbo, you can be the leader.

02:09:51.690 --> 02:09:52.730
You stay there.

02:09:52.970 --> 02:09:53.950
Oh, all right.

02:09:54.550 --> 02:09:57.460
Fair, I'm really hungry.

02:09:57.740 --> 02:09:59.520
I want to eat a cracker now.

02:10:01.560 --> 02:10:04.060
Please, walk here. Ready?

02:10:08.290 --> 02:10:12.470
Now, who can I see moving? Nobody.

02:10:13.190 --> 02:10:14.130
Oh, for you.

02:10:16.370 --> 02:10:17.580
Who's moving?

02:10:18.160 --> 02:10:20.440
Oh, smelly-jilly. I'm out.

02:10:22.540 --> 02:10:23.940
Oh, bad luck.

02:10:24.810 --> 02:10:27.710
I just want everyone to hurry up.

02:10:30.800 --> 02:10:32.660
Oh, good. They're nearly here.

02:10:34.420 --> 02:10:40.240
Oh, I bet you've got me. Your turn now.

02:10:40.680 --> 02:10:42.540
I've got me now.

02:10:42.970 --> 02:10:43.310
Ready?

02:10:46.930 --> 02:10:51.400
What are you doing?

02:10:56.810 --> 02:10:58.690
Oh, doing?

02:11:00.000 --> 02:11:03.420
I needed something to eat

02:11:03.760 --> 02:11:07.010
Oh, hello there, everyone

02:11:07.010 --> 02:11:08.570
What's for tea?

02:11:08.950 --> 02:11:10.250
Oh, hello, Roly

02:11:10.250 --> 02:11:13.490
Oh, Roly, this is Rimbo

02:11:13.490 --> 02:11:15.110
He's come for tea, too

02:11:15.110 --> 02:11:17.430
Oh, hello there, Rimbo

02:11:17.430 --> 02:11:19.040
Do you like stories?

02:11:19.380 --> 02:11:21.800
Yes, Roly, let's have a story

02:11:21.800 --> 02:11:23.720
Then we can have tea

02:11:24.060 --> 02:11:25.580
Yes, tea

02:11:25.580 --> 02:11:29.890
Right-o, back in a Roly-mo

02:11:30.000 --> 02:11:39.080
When you take a look inside a book, who knows what you will see?

02:11:39.480 --> 02:11:45.800
When you take a look inside a book, it's fun as fun can be.

02:11:46.340 --> 02:11:58.980
With cats and dogs and birds and frogs, a monkey who says boo, boo, wonderful things, giants and kings, and maybe a thimble or two.

02:12:00.060 --> 02:12:00.880
What have we here?

02:12:01.340 --> 02:12:07.220
When you take a look inside a book, who knows what you might see?

02:12:07.620 --> 02:12:13.910
A story or rhyme, just take the time to read along with me.

02:12:14.150 --> 02:12:19.370
Are you sitting comfortably?

02:12:19.570 --> 02:12:20.210
Oh, yes.

02:12:21.030 --> 02:12:21.770
Then I'll begin.

02:12:22.170 --> 02:12:26.730
This story is called Little Red Riding Hood.

02:12:29.050 --> 02:12:29.890
Once upon a time.

02:12:30.380 --> 02:12:34.520
There was a little girl, and everyone called her Little Red Riding Hood.

02:12:35.440 --> 02:12:38.880
One day, her mother said, I've made some buns for your grandma.

02:12:39.270 --> 02:12:40.450
Will you take them too, huh?

02:12:41.420 --> 02:12:46.900
A visit to grandma was always exciting, because she would sometimes play tricks on her granddaughter.

02:12:47.680 --> 02:12:50.360
So, off dashed Little Red Riding Hood.

02:12:51.230 --> 02:12:56.290
In the forest, two friendly rabbits ran in front of her, but suddenly they vanished.

02:12:56.490 --> 02:12:59.910
And there was Wolf hanging upside down in a tree.

02:13:00.000 --> 02:13:04.300
Oh, wolf, she said. You scared those rabbits.

02:13:05.080 --> 02:13:09.250
Ho, ho, ho, grinned the wolf. He enjoyed scaring rabbits.

02:13:09.820 --> 02:13:11.740
What have you got in your basket?

02:13:12.490 --> 02:13:15.360
Buns for Grandma, said Little Red Riding Hood.

02:13:16.050 --> 02:13:18.810
Not for you. And she went on her way.

02:13:19.720 --> 02:13:22.700
When she reached Grandma's cottage, she stepped inside.

02:13:23.630 --> 02:13:25.280
Granny, where are you?

02:13:25.920 --> 02:13:28.820
I'm in bed, came the gruff reply.

02:13:30.000 --> 02:13:34.430
sound like grandma thought Little Red Riding Hood she went into the bedroom

02:13:34.430 --> 02:13:41.440
your eyes look very large today grandma she said all the better to see you with

02:13:41.440 --> 02:13:48.890
my dear and your nose it's very large too all the better to smell those lovely

02:13:48.890 --> 02:13:56.160
buns you've brought me grandma your mouth is huge too all the better to eat

02:13:56.640 --> 02:13:59.340
Eat what? said Little Red Riding Hood.

02:14:00.120 --> 02:14:02.880
Just then, the door was flung wide open.

02:14:03.180 --> 02:14:05.980
It was Grandma, and she was laughing.

02:14:06.530 --> 02:14:08.130
Grandma pulled back the curtains.

02:14:09.100 --> 02:14:10.240
The wolf sat up.

02:14:10.400 --> 02:14:16.340
He was dressed in Grandma's best nightdress and cap, and he was laughing.

02:14:17.160 --> 02:14:20.240
Now, he said, may I have one of those buns?

02:14:21.900 --> 02:14:27.410
So Grandma, Little Red Riding Hood, and the wolf had the buns for tea.

02:14:30.120 --> 02:14:33.820
Do you think the wolf was wearing a wig when he was pretending to be Grandma?

02:14:34.480 --> 02:14:36.890
Yes, Flory, I think he was.

02:14:37.840 --> 02:14:39.120
I must be off.

02:14:40.420 --> 02:14:42.720
It must be tea time now.

02:14:43.960 --> 02:14:47.440
I want to try the mud bridge first.

02:14:47.860 --> 02:14:49.120
No, thank you.

02:14:49.500 --> 02:14:51.460
What about a stick biscuit?

02:14:51.840 --> 02:14:54.980
No, I want a cracker.

02:14:57.420 --> 02:14:59.980
Oh, sorry, Rimbo, but I...

02:15:00.000 --> 02:15:03.460
I'm saving those for Fimbo. They're his favourite.

02:15:03.720 --> 02:15:04.440
Yes, they are.

02:15:04.580 --> 02:15:06.860
But I...and Fimbo.

02:15:07.920 --> 02:15:09.620
It doesn't have pink hair.

02:15:09.800 --> 02:15:10.080
No.

02:15:10.690 --> 02:15:15.150
Oh, it is me. I'm wearing a wig. A pink wig.

02:15:19.380 --> 02:15:22.740
Oh, wiggy, wiggy, wig, wig.

02:15:23.020 --> 02:15:26.560
Um, Flory, can I please have a cracker now?

02:15:26.800 --> 02:15:29.980
Oh, of course you can, Fimbo. Or do I...

02:15:30.000 --> 02:15:31.600
I mean RIMBO!

02:15:32.710 --> 02:15:35.250
RIMBO, RIMBO, RIMBO, FIMBO!

02:15:35.450 --> 02:15:35.950
Yay!

02:15:38.110 --> 02:15:41.980
Where have all the crackers gone?

02:15:42.660 --> 02:15:45.060
Frogs like crumble crackers too, Fimbo!

02:15:46.360 --> 02:15:47.060
Rockies!

02:15:47.680 --> 02:15:48.760
Yubby, yubby, yum, yum!

02:16:08.090 --> 02:16:14.720
little chickadee. The Fimbo's had a busy day today. Who found the pink wig first?

02:16:15.720 --> 02:16:16.920
That's right.

02:16:17.670 --> 02:16:27.620
Were Fimbo, weren't it? Fimbo found something pink and sparkly. It thought it were a huck.

02:16:29.620 --> 02:16:29.980
But what?

02:16:30.000 --> 02:16:30.920
What was it really?

02:16:32.410 --> 02:16:35.010
That's right, you clever little fluffy love.

02:16:35.370 --> 02:16:37.030
Yes, it was a wig.

02:16:38.100 --> 02:16:41.880
But I put it on and pretended to be RIMBO.

02:16:44.350 --> 02:16:46.600
Can you remember the song they sang?

02:16:49.640 --> 02:16:50.040
That's right.

02:16:50.800 --> 02:16:54.510
Hello, hello, wouldn't you like to come to tea?

02:16:54.710 --> 02:16:56.590
There's tea for you and tea for me.

02:16:56.790 --> 02:16:58.750
Lots to drink and lots to eat.

02:16:59.050 --> 02:16:59.790
Come for tea.

02:17:00.120 --> 02:17:07.810
special treat. Maybe you can find something to dress up in and make you look different

02:17:07.810 --> 02:17:13.540
too. Come and find us next time, won't you? I must fly. Goodbye.

02:17:38.830 --> 02:17:49.770
Pig, this is my little brother George, this is mommy pig, and this is daddy pig, the pig.

02:18:01.850 --> 02:18:05.930
Peppa and George are going to the playgroup. It is George's first day.

02:18:06.490 --> 02:18:09.240
George, are you looking forward to the playgroup?

02:18:09.890 --> 02:18:15.330
D, maybe George is to go to my playgroup.

02:18:16.360 --> 02:18:21.520
He'll be fine, Peppa. There'll be you and Mr. Dinosaur there to keep him company.

02:18:22.140 --> 02:18:23.820
Grr, dinosaur.

02:18:25.380 --> 02:18:27.970
But I want to play with the big children.

02:18:28.370 --> 02:18:29.970
Not George and his toy.

02:18:30.060 --> 02:18:31.000
Binosaur.

02:18:31.500 --> 02:18:32.100
Oh dear.

02:18:32.540 --> 02:18:34.780
Peppa doesn't want George to go to her playgroup.

02:18:41.410 --> 02:18:42.030
We're here!

02:18:43.980 --> 02:18:44.300
Ready?

02:18:45.170 --> 02:18:46.850
Sure George is big enough.

02:18:47.450 --> 02:18:48.610
He'll be fine.

02:18:52.200 --> 02:18:52.480
Right.

02:18:53.390 --> 02:18:54.050
He can come.

02:18:56.330 --> 02:18:57.270
Bye-bye!

02:19:05.740 --> 02:19:08.800
Madame Gazelle looks after the children at the playgroup.

02:19:09.680 --> 02:19:14.600
My little brother George.

02:19:15.900 --> 02:19:17.560
Hello, George.

02:19:19.130 --> 02:19:27.540
I wish I had a little brother like George.

02:19:27.880 --> 02:19:28.460
Really?

02:19:29.650 --> 02:19:29.890
Hello.

02:19:30.000 --> 02:19:31.180
Hello, I'm Danny Dog.

02:19:31.660 --> 02:19:33.540
Is that a dinosaur?

02:19:34.350 --> 02:19:36.420
It's just a toy dinosaur.

02:19:37.240 --> 02:19:39.220
Grrrr. Dinosaur.

02:19:39.850 --> 02:19:40.690
Brilliant.

02:19:41.430 --> 02:19:43.560
Grrrr. Dinosaur.

02:19:44.040 --> 02:19:44.780
Grrrr.

02:19:48.310 --> 02:19:50.420
Dinosaur. Grrrr.

02:19:50.650 --> 02:19:52.830
Ah, really scary.

02:19:54.470 --> 02:19:55.890
That's brilliant.

02:19:57.560 --> 02:19:59.180
George is my brother.

02:20:00.060 --> 02:20:00.990
He's brilliant.

02:20:02.730 --> 02:20:04.850
Peppa is proud of her little brother, George.

02:20:08.820 --> 02:20:12.180
Shall we show George how we paint pictures?

02:20:12.830 --> 02:20:14.770
George is not very good at painting.

02:20:15.430 --> 02:20:17.490
Well, maybe you could help him.

02:20:18.170 --> 02:20:20.480
Yes, I'm very good.

02:20:20.680 --> 02:20:23.150
We'll show him how to paint a flower.

02:20:24.300 --> 02:20:28.590
George, today I'm going to teach you how to paint a flower.

02:20:31.120 --> 02:20:52.910
First you paint a big circle George, that's the wrong colour. Paint the flowers petals. George, that's the wrong shape. Paint the storm.

02:21:01.530 --> 02:21:03.530
George, you've done it all wrong.

02:21:06.210 --> 02:21:07.830
Now, what do we have here?

02:21:10.360 --> 02:21:12.400
That's very good, Peppa.

02:21:13.360 --> 02:21:16.460
And George has painted a dinosaur.

02:21:18.800 --> 02:21:19.480
Dinosaur.

02:21:22.770 --> 02:21:23.450
Brilliant.

02:21:26.120 --> 02:21:29.840
I think George and Peppa's pictures should go on the wall.

02:21:33.750 --> 02:21:37.610
Peppa, you must be very proud of your little brother

02:21:38.020 --> 02:21:40.060
Yes, I am

02:21:42.170 --> 02:21:46.690
It is home time and the children's parents are here to pick them up

02:21:47.800 --> 02:21:49.860
Can George come next time?

02:21:50.440 --> 02:21:53.720
Yes, and he can paint us another lovely picture

02:21:53.720 --> 02:21:57.200
And what will you paint next time, George?

02:21:58.000 --> 02:21:58.980
I'm sure

02:22:00.000 --> 02:22:02.920
Oh, another dinosaur picture.

02:22:03.290 --> 02:22:06.450
Well, maybe you can show us all how to paint a dinosaur.

02:22:08.250 --> 02:22:09.110
Brilliant.

02:22:10.080 --> 02:22:11.750
Yes, brilliant.

02:22:13.340 --> 02:22:14.020
Brilliant.

02:22:31.120 --> 02:22:32.160
Bye.

02:23:17.980 --> 02:23:24.720
In summer, the gangers cut the long grass on the lion side, raking it into heaps to dry in the sun.

02:23:26.200 --> 02:23:29.260
This time of year, Percy stops where they have been cutting.

02:23:32.200 --> 02:23:35.620
The men load up his empty wagons and he pulls them to the station.

02:23:44.080 --> 02:23:47.360
Toby then takes them to the hills for the farmers to feed their stock.

02:24:02.590 --> 02:24:07.420
Percy gave a ghostly whistle.

02:24:08.210 --> 02:24:10.310
Don't be frightened, Thomas, he laughed.

02:24:10.610 --> 02:24:11.470
It's only me.

02:24:12.010 --> 02:24:15.310
Your ugly fizz is enough to frighten anyone, said Thomas.

02:24:15.530 --> 02:24:17.510
You're like ugly indeed.

02:24:17.730 --> 02:24:22.490
I'm a green caterpillar with red stripes, continued Thomas firmly.

02:24:22.960 --> 02:24:24.360
You crawl like one too.

02:24:25.050 --> 02:24:25.830
I don't.

02:24:26.500 --> 02:24:28.660
Who's been late every afternoon this week?

02:24:29.180 --> 02:24:29.920
It's the hay.

02:24:30.000 --> 02:24:32.340
I can't help that, said Thomas.

02:24:32.820 --> 02:24:36.360
Time's time, and the Fat Controller relies on me to keep it.

02:24:36.950 --> 02:24:39.530
I can't if you crawl in the hay till all hours.

02:24:40.270 --> 02:24:43.790
Green Caterpillar indeed, fumed Percy.

02:24:44.070 --> 02:24:47.350
He set off to collect some hay, take to the harbour.

02:24:49.120 --> 02:24:52.660
Everyone says I'm handsome, or at least nearly everyone.

02:24:53.390 --> 02:24:56.290
Anyway, my curves are better than Thomas' corners.

02:24:57.670 --> 02:24:59.970
Thomas says I'm always late, he grumbled.

02:25:00.060 --> 02:25:03.780
I'm never late, or at least only a few minutes.

02:25:04.340 --> 02:25:05.360
What's that to Thomas?

02:25:05.790 --> 02:25:08.070
He can always catch up time further on.

02:25:08.800 --> 02:25:12.700
All the same, he and his driver decided to start home early.

02:25:13.550 --> 02:25:14.590
Then came trouble.

02:25:15.210 --> 02:25:24.510
A crate of treacle was upset all over Percy.

02:25:29.060 --> 02:25:29.960
Percy was cr-

02:25:30.000 --> 02:25:40.690
cross. He was still sticky when he puffed away. The wind was blowing fiercely. Look

02:25:40.690 --> 02:25:47.320
at that, exclaimed the driver. The wind caught the piled hay, tossing it up and over the

02:25:47.320 --> 02:25:54.300
track. The lion climbed here. Take a run at it, Percy, his driver advised. Percy gathered

02:25:54.300 --> 02:25:59.210
speed, but the hay made the rails slippery and his wheels wouldn't grip.

02:26:00.190 --> 02:26:07.610
Time after time, he stalled with spinning wheels and had to wait till the line ahead was cleared before he could start again.

02:26:11.760 --> 02:26:15.520
Everyone was waiting. Thomas seethed impatiently.

02:26:16.010 --> 02:26:20.630
Ten minutes late, I warned him, passengers will complain and the fat controller.

02:26:21.620 --> 02:26:25.380
Then they all saw Percy. They laughed and shouted.

02:26:31.310 --> 02:26:33.530
Sorry I'm late, Percy panted.

02:26:34.240 --> 02:26:37.140
Look what's crawled out of the hay, tears Thomas.

02:26:38.060 --> 02:26:39.300
What's wrong, asked Percy.

02:26:39.960 --> 02:26:42.440
Talk about hairy caterpillars, puffed Thomas.

02:26:42.720 --> 02:26:44.920
It's worth being late to have seen you.

02:26:53.000 --> 02:26:56.700
When Percy got home, his driver showed him what he looked like in a mirror.

02:26:59.400 --> 02:26:59.980
Bust my...

02:27:00.000 --> 02:27:06.150
buffers no wonder they all laughed I'm just like a woolly bear please clean me

02:27:06.150 --> 02:27:25.020
before Toby comes but it was no good Thomas told Toby all about it instead of

02:27:25.020 --> 02:27:29.770
talking about sensible things like playing ghosts Thomas and Toby made

02:27:30.000 --> 02:27:34.500
jokes about woolly bear caterpillars and other creatures which crawl about in hay.

02:27:35.360 --> 02:27:40.110
They laughed a lot, but Percy thought they were really being very silly indeed.

02:28:00.380 --> 02:28:00.520
We'll be right back.

02:29:05.630 --> 02:29:09.390
The chief controller was on the telephone receiving rather disturbing news.

02:29:09.730 --> 02:29:15.640
The airport administration had decided to add another Jimbo to their fleet of aeroplane.

02:29:16.380 --> 02:29:19.410
But sir, I wish you would reconsider your proposal.

02:29:19.980 --> 02:29:22.310
No, but you've made their minds up, Chief.

02:29:23.100 --> 02:29:26.850
More asset to this airport, despite his legal size.

02:29:27.350 --> 02:29:29.850
But sir, to build another Jimbo.

02:29:30.000 --> 02:29:33.990
Yes, sir. Of course, sir. Right away, sir.

02:29:34.880 --> 02:29:38.040
Tommy Tow Truck, take Jimbo down to the aircraft factory.

02:29:38.300 --> 02:29:41.940
They want to measure him up and make another one exactly like him.

02:29:42.100 --> 02:29:43.860
Oh, no, it's too much.

02:29:44.600 --> 02:29:46.340
He sounds a little upset, Tommy.

02:29:46.690 --> 02:29:51.210
It's just that the chief doesn't think that this airport can go up with two Jimbo's.

02:29:51.600 --> 02:29:53.500
I'm inclined to agree with him.

02:29:55.030 --> 02:29:58.990
Now then, as chief designer of this project, I want no mistake this time.

02:29:59.310 --> 02:29:59.870
